  "text": "NICE Guideline CG150: Headaches in Over 12s Diagnosis and Management | Publisher: National\nHeadache Red Flags Requiring Immediate Emergency Referral\nUrgent Red Flags (SNOOP Criteria): - Sudden onset severe headache reaching\npeak intensity within seconds ('thunderclap' headache). - Headache\naccompanied by fever, stiff neck, confusion, seizure, or focal\nneurological deficits (weakness, numbness, vision loss). - New headache in\npatients with history of cancer or immunocompromise. - Headache associated\nwith recent head trauma or worsening with coughing/straining. -\nProgressive headache worsening over days or weeks in adults over 50.\nPage 2 of 4 | Official Educational Resource",
